{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"deistic-conventual-blackmamba","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nWhen a `Gerrit Verified Gate` run is CANCELLED — normally because a new patchset superseded it via\na concurrency group — the CI bot votes **`Verified-1`** under the headline **\"FAILURE\"**, and only\nthen, in a separate follow-up message, states that the job was *\"CANCELLED (not a test verdict)\"*.\n\nThe vote and its headline assert a test failure that did not occur. The correcting detail arrives\nas a second message that a reader has to notice and connect.\n\n## Evidence — change 2683, 2026-09-05\n\n```\n21:21:03  Rebar Bot Nava   Uploaded patch set 3.\n21:21:07  (run 33992792776 STARTS for PS3)\n21:21:58  rebar CI bot     Patch Set 2: Verified-1\n                           FAILURE: .../actions/runs/33991673464\n21:22:00  rebar CI bot     Patch Set 2:\n                           CI did not pass. Jobs that did not succeed:\n                           - build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.13):\n                             CANCELLED (not a test verdict) after 20m59s\n```\n\nRun states confirm the mechanism:\n\n```\n33991673464  created 20:58:49  completed  cancelled     <- PS2's run\n33992792776  created 21:21:07  in_progress              <- PS3's run, started FIRST\n```\n\nThe PS2 run was cancelled 56 seconds AFTER the PS3 run started — a concurrency-group cancellation\ncaused by the author's own supersede, which is correct and expected behaviour. Nothing failed.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing\n\nThe bot already KNOWS the distinction — it prints \"not a test verdict\" verbatim. What it does not\ndo is let that distinction reach the vote, which is the artifact every human and agent reads first.\n\nObserved cost in a single session:\n- An agent had to investigate its own change's `-1` to establish there was no failure to triage.\n- The orchestrator was one step from delegating a non-existent CI failure for root-causing.\n- CONTRIBUTING.md reserves `recheck` for provably environmental faults and requires the reasoning\n  be stated. A `-1` labelled FAILURE invites exactly the reflexive `recheck` that rule exists to\n  prevent — and here a fresh run was already in flight, so a recheck would have added a third\n  concurrent run under load.\n\n## Suggested direction (not prescriptive)\n\nA cancelled run is an ABSENCE of a verdict, not a negative one. Options, in rough order of\npreference:\n1. Do not vote at all on cancellation — leave the label at 0 and post the explanatory message. A\n   superseding run is already underway and will vote.\n2. Vote 0 explicitly with the cancellation reason.\n3. Keep the `-1` but change the headline from \"FAILURE\" to name cancellation, so vote and detail\n   at least agree.\n\nDistinguish SUPERSESSION-cancellation from an operator-cancelled or infrastructure-killed run if\nthat is cheap; both are \"no verdict\", but only the first is routine.\n\n## Relationship to sibling findings\n\nThis is the third instance in one session of a check reporting \"I could not determine\" as \"I\ndetermined the bad outcome\":\n- `erratic-sunny-genet` — Mirror Guard reports `healthy: false` on an IO/TLS failure that prevented\n  it reaching the host at all; the mirror was verifiably in sync.\n- Change 2683 itself — CloudWatch alarms with `treat_missing_data = breaching` and\n  `datapoints_to_alarm < evaluation_periods`, where absent buckets out-vote a real healthy\n  datapoint. Four fired simultaneously at 20:47Z on healthy infrastructure.\n- This bug.\n\nThe shared remedy shape is the same in all three: report inability-to-measure as its OWN signal\nrather than folding it into the measured verdict.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A cancelled `Gerrit Verified Gate` run does not produce a vote and headline that assert a\n      test failure.\n- [ ] AC2 Genuine CI failures are unaffected — a real red suite must still vote `Verified-1`. Prove\n      both branches, not just the changed one.\n- [ ] AC3 The cancellation reason remains visible on the change; this must not become silence.\n- [ ] AC4 A test covers cancelled and failed runs distinctly.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (exit 127) —\nbound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Terraform may be written and validated but NEVER\napplied. Do not touch the shared main checkout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","id":"d1d4-8c8b-e2c5-4ac2","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"CI bot votes Verified-1 'FAILURE' on a superseded/cancelled run, then says 'not a test verdict'"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788644779894756001,"uuid":"d2ebc9d1-1d49-4907-97e1-d3b65edb4a32"}